The {{Term/Store|Evil Spirit Greaves||Series, TotK}},{{Exp Game|TotK}}<ref name="TotK Inventory"/> also known as the {{Term/Store|Phantom Ganon Greaves||BotW}},{{Exp Game|BotW}}<ref name="BotW Inventory"/> are a recurring [[Item]] in {{TLoZ Series}}.

==Location and Uses==
==={{BotW|-}}===
{{Descriptions BotW}}
The Phantom Ganon Greaves are a piece of [[Armor]] exclusive to {{TCB}} [[Downloadable Content]] pack. Obtaining the Phantom Ganon Greaves is one part of the objective of the "[[EX Treasure: Dark Armor]]" [[Side Quest]]. The Greaves were stolen from [[Hyrule Castle (Dungeon)|Hyrule Castle]] by [[Misko]] and a clue to their location can be found in ''[[Misko's EX Journal 2]]'' at the [[Deya Village Ruins]].<ref name="BotW Misko's EX Journal 2"/><ref name="BotW Misko's EX Journal 2 2"/> The metallic [[Treasure Chest]] that hides the Phantom Ganon Greaves can be found buried in the ground near a bird statue in [[Ebara Forest]]. Link must use the [[Magnesis]] [[Rune]] to dislodge the Chest from the ground to retrieve the Greaves.

When worn, the Greaves provide one level of [[Stealth Up]]. The Phantom Ganon Greaves cannot be enhanced by a [[Great Fairy]] nor can they be [[Dye]]d at the [[Kochi Dye Shop]]. The Phantom Ganon Greaves, alongside the [[Phantom Ganon Skull]] and [[Phantom Ganon Armor]], compose the [[Phantom Ganon Set]].

According to their description, it is believed that the Phantom Ganon Greaves are infused with a [[Phantom Ganon|dark entity]] that resembles the [[Ganon|Great King of Evil]].<ref name="BotW Inventory"/> After obtaining the Phantom Ganon Greaves, [[Granté]] in [[Tarrey Town]] will begin selling them for 50 [[Rupee]]s.

